  "configuration_id": "config_001",
  "reason": "1) Evidence/uncertainty: No experiments have been completed, so there is no baseline performance to reference. The most critical uncertainty is the performance floor of the simplest RNA-only model, which will calibrate whether more complex design choices (learned encoders, multiprofile aggregation, multimodal fusion) actually add value. 2) What this tests: config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is the simplest configuration in the search space—a standard PCA reduction with no learned encoder, no aggregation, and no fusion. It establishes the baseline accuracy/F1 for RNA-based classification under the most minimal pipeline. 3) Why it is the best use of the first experiment: Starting with the simplest baseline is the highest-information first step because it anchors all subsequent comparisons. Every later experiment (multiprofile, scvi/scgpt encoders, image-only, multimodal) will be interpreted relative to this floor. Without it, we cannot tell whether a 2-3% gain from a complex multimodal model is meaningful or just noise. It also avoids the risk of over-investing in a complex configuration before knowing whether the simpler signal is already sufficient."
}

